WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.450
When gas prices jump, most
drivers still fill up their tanks.

2
00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:09.700
Researchers found drivers reacted
even less from 2001 to 2006

3
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.870
than from 1975 to 1980.

4
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:15.360
But raise the price of one brand of snack,

5
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.750
and its buyers can disappear.

6
00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.420
So why do some buyers barely
react when a price jumps,

7
00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.660
while others switch away at once?

8
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.170
In this mission, you'll calculate
the price elasticity of demand

9
00:00:27.170 --> 00:00:28.790
with the midpoint method.

10
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.430
Then you'll slide a point
along a demand curve

11
00:00:31.430 --> 00:00:33.590
and read off its elasticity.

12
00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:37.880
Your mission: explain what
decides how strongly buyers react.
